ate_int_coverage":null,"_gp_int_coverage":null,"_score_int_coverage":null,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":-0.07013207526893275,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":88.7,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.6048735732322941,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.06523018999390348,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":18.5,"_gate_piotroski":8,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":88.9,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.04856480294383125,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":59.4,"_gate_rev_durability":0.22206570813101645,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.00958167432384141,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":21.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.004297675392277656,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":55.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010691103474608629,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":82.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.00299,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Cboe Global Markets, Inc., through its subsidiaries, operates as a derivatives and securities exchange network that delivers trading, clearing, and investment solutions in the United States and internationally. It operates through five segments: Options, North American Equities, Europe and Asia Pacific, Futures, and Global FX. The Options segment includes options on market indices, stocks of individual corporations, and exchange-traded products (ETPs), such as exchange-traded funds (ETFs) and exchange-traded notes (ETNs). This segment also offers trading in listed options through a single system. The North American Equities segment comprises U.S. equities and ETP transaction services. This segment also includes listing services on Cboe Canada, ETP listings on BZX, the Cboe Global Markets, Inc. common stock listing, and applicable market data. The Europe and Asia Pacific segment provides pan-European derivatives transaction services; ETPs, including exchange-traded funds, exchange-traded notes, and exchange-traded commodities; international depository receipts; and an ETP listings business on regulated markets and clearing activities, as well as equities services. The Futures segment offers transaction services, including trading in VIX futures and other futures products, the licensing of proprietary market data, and access and capacity services. The Global FX segment provides institutional foreign exchange (FX) trading and non-deliverable forward FX transaction services. The company also provides trading solutions and products in multiple asset classes, including equities, derivatives, and FX across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific. It has strategic relationships with S&P Dow Jones Indices, LLC; Frank Russell Company; and FTSE International Limited. The company was formerly known as CBOE Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to Cboe Global Markets, Inc. in October 2017. Cboe Global Markets, Inc. was founded in 1973 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Craig Steven Donohue | CEO, President & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $3.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $2.8M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 17%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $1.0M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $30K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Cboe Global Markets, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $36.6B market cap on $4.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +22% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 7% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 45%.","The business throws off $1.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 36 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.59\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 28\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Carries a 67% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6735336194563664},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 15% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Financial Services peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"CBOE Bets on Prediction Markets to Broaden Its Retail Footprint","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036757/cboe-bets-on-prediction-markets-to-broaden-its-retail-footprint?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cquick_take-3036757","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795794060.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cboe Clear Europe Sets Annual Record for Client Equity Trades Cleared","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/cboe-clear-europe-sets-annual-record-for-client-equity-trades-cleared-302949882.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795593600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.459,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (CBOE) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_CBOE_Edition_112426011602_1795544162.html","date":"2026-11-